# Example B1 with a kaon- beam and everything QBBC gives a negative kaon that this port does
# not have, switched off. The P1 stage; see muon_emonly.mac for why each line is here.
#
# `ref/oracle/species_processes.csv` for kaon- is pi-'s list with kaon-Inelastic in place of
# pi-Inelastic: the same ICRU73QO low-energy model, the same hBertiniCaptureAtRest, the same
# seven inactivations. A stopped K- is captured and not decayed, for the reason
# pion_minus_emonly.mac gives.
#
# MEASURED, 500,000 events:
#
#   kaon-  port 1239.62 +/- 1.303 nGy   Geant4 1131.87 +/- 1.195   +9.52%, 61.0 sigma
#   kaon+  port 1242.97 +/- 1.306 nGy   Geant4 1240.74 +/- 1.302   +0.18%, 1.21 sigma
#
# The largest charge-odd split of the three species measured, and the slowest particle of the
# three at 200 MeV: beta 0.703 against the pion's 0.911 and the muon's 0.938. The order is
# mu- 3.78%, pi- 5.01%, kaon- 9.52% - monotone in mass at fixed kinetic energy, which is
# monotone in 1/beta. Geant4's own kaon dE/dx table has kaon- 0.29% ABOVE kaon+ in water, so
# the sign of the table's split is opposite to the sign of the dose's. docs/RISK.md.
#
# 200 MeV kaon-: 408.8 mm of water (hadron_tables.csv, G4_WATER at 199.5262 MeV), so it crosses
# B1's 300 mm envelope. NOTE this corrects kaon_emonly.mac's header beside it, which says
# "about 14 cm of water" and that the stopped kaon decays inside the phantom - the kaon at this
# energy does not stop in B1 at all.

/run/initialize
/control/verbose 0
/run/verbose 1

/process/inactivate hadElastic
/process/inactivate kaon-Inelastic
/process/inactivate Decay
/process/inactivate hBertiniCaptureAtRest
/process/inactivate hBrems
/process/inactivate hPairProd
/process/inactivate CoulombScat

/gun/particle kaon-
/gun/energy 200 MeV

/run/printProgress 100000
/run/beamOn 500000
